{"sourceSha256": "9a77baa73249556f6891346ebde263a4c8719c0572f793c89b8ecd83eae152b5", "text": "© ¥i ta “Tl\n\nOET Online: Writing Feedback\n\nCriteria | Needs work | Satisfactory | Strong\nPurpose v\nContent v\n‘Conciseness | | v\n& Clarity\nGenre & v\nStyle |\nOrganisation v\n& Layout |\nLanguage v\nOverall | Good work. You managed to extract most of the main points for this\n\nComments letter\n\nThis is actually a tricky letter as it contains a lot of information which may\nnot be required for the reader. You need to understand that this is a letter\nto an occupational therapist. In case notes, there was a lot of information\ngiven but the ones that were most relevant to the reader of this letter\nwere:\ne Conservative management: night-time wrist splinting (for >3\nweeks) You got this right!\n@ Refer to occupational therapy for wrist splint (custom-made, in\nneutral position) & ergonomics assessment You got this right\n\nTake note, since an ergonomics assessment is required, the relevant\ninformation that need to be included would be\n\ne Supermarket manager You got this right!\n\n¢ Job: ‘v tiring’ You got this right\n\ne long hours, ‘on feet all day’ | added this for you even though | am\n\naware that her problem is with her right hand, not her feet\nHowever, the expression ‘on her feet all day’ actually means that\n\nshe is working non-stop\n\nThis sample question is actually good practice on a different type of\nsituation which you may get in your exam. If you ever get something like\nthis in your exam, keep these things in mind:\n\n¢ Who am! writing to?\n\ne What do! want her to do?\n\ne What does she need to know to do her job?\n\nGood work on this one\n\n~ ~ ORT Online\nh Website: http://oetonline.net.au\n\nGrade: B (360)\nThis is a pass but since you need 400, you have to be careful with the little\ndetails. You do not have to change all the words given in the case notes\n(e.g. you can maintain ‘grip strength’) as long as you can construct good\nsentences with them. Sometimes using the words in the case notes will\nmake more sense and can help you write faster as well (and leave you\nwith some time for proofreading).", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "© ¥i ta “Tl\n\nOET Online: Writing Feedback\n\nCriteria | Needs work | Satisfactory | Strong\nPurpose v\nContent v\n‘Conciseness | | v\n& Clarity\nGenre & v\nStyle |\nOrganisation v\n& Layout |\nLanguage v\nOverall | Good work. You managed to extract most of the main points for this\n\nComments letter\n\nThis is actually a tricky letter as it contains a lot of information which may\nnot be required for the reader. You need to understand that this is a letter\nto an occupational therapist. In case notes, there was a lot of information\ngiven but the ones that were most relevant to the reader of this letter\nwere:\ne Conservative management: night-time wrist splinting (for >3\nweeks) You got this right!\n@ Refer to occupational therapy for wrist splint (custom-made, in\nneutral position) & ergonomics assessment You got this right\n\nTake note, since an ergonomics assessment is required, the relevant\ninformation that need to be included would be\n\ne Supermarket manager You got this right!\n\n¢ Job: ‘v tiring’ You got this right\n\ne long hours, ‘on feet all day’ | added this for you even though | am\n\naware that her problem is with her right hand, not her feet\nHowever, the expression ‘on her feet all day’ actually means that\n\nshe is working non-stop\n\nThis sample question is actually good practice on a different type of\nsituation which you may get in your exam. If you ever get something like\nthis in your exam, keep these things in mind:\n\n¢ Who am! writing to?\n\ne What do! want her to do?\n\ne What does she need to know to do her job?\n\nGood work on this one\n\n~ ~ ORT Online\nh Website: http://oetonline.net.au\n\nGrade: B (360)\nThis is a pass but since you need 400, you have to be careful with the little\ndetails. You do not have to change all the words given 